WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.017
Applying for jobs is mostly retyping.

00:00:03.017 --> 00:00:07.046
The same details, into a different form, every time.

00:00:07.346 --> 00:00:11.874
This is the app that stops that. Here is the whole thing.

00:00:12.174 --> 00:00:17.011
You fill in your details once. Name, phone, address.

00:00:17.311 --> 00:00:23.119
Add your résumé and a photo. No signature saved? It draws one from your name.

00:00:23.419 --> 00:00:27.548
No résumé yet? Rough notes in, a written résumé out.

00:00:27.848 --> 00:00:31.778
Then pick the format for where you are applying.

00:00:31.778 --> 00:00:34.316
A German CV is not a US résumé.

00:00:34.616 --> 00:00:39.743
Now the jobs. You search the live web from inside the app.

00:00:39.743 --> 00:00:41.776
Real, current listings.

00:00:42.076 --> 00:00:45.751
One tap pulls the whole posting in, and saves it.

00:00:46.051 --> 00:00:49.099
It reads the role, researches the company,

00:00:49.099 --> 00:00:52.583
and writes a cover letter for that specific job.

00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:56.125
Pick your region, download as PDF or Word.

00:00:56.425 --> 00:00:59.102
Then the part that saves real time.

00:00:59.102 --> 00:01:02.772
Open the employer's own form, and tap the robot.

00:01:03.072 --> 00:01:05.230
It fills the whole thing in.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:09.393
Details, dropdowns, the questions your résumé answers.

00:01:09.693 --> 00:01:14.708
Your files attach themselves. Submit, and it is logged on your dashboard.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.187
So that is the whole loop.

00:01:17.187 --> 00:01:21.794
Find a job, and apply, without typing it all out again.

00:01:22.094 --> 00:01:26.274
CVApplyr. Free to start, on iPhone and Android.

